// Copy to Configs/Local.xcconfig (gitignored) to sign Debug builds with your own certificate.
//
// Why: macOS remembers privacy grants such as "access files in your Documents folder" against the
// app's signature. An ad hoc signature changes with every build, so each rebuild asks again. A build
// signed with an Apple Development certificate keeps the same identity and keeps the grant.
//
// `security find-identity -v -p codesigning` lists the identities on this Mac. The certificate has to
// belong to the team in DEVELOPMENT_TEAM (Project.swift); set it here as well if yours differs.
// Manual style signs with the certificate alone, so no provisioning profile is needed.
//
// Command-line overrides still win: Scripts/ci.sh and CI pass CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY=- where they
// need an ad hoc build.

MIMIC_CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = Apple Development
CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Manual
// DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = XXXXXXXXXX
